  "summary": "Senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore from the Nick Xenophon Team is resigning due to her dual British citizenship, which she inherited from her mother. Kakoschke-Moore was unaware of her British citizenship until recently, as she had previously believed she was not eligible. Her mother's birth in Singapore and subsequent British citizenship in 1983 conferred the same citizenship to Kakoschke-Moore by descent. She plans to refer the matter to the high court and hopes to return to the Senate. A recount of the 2016 Senate election is likely to elect Tim Storrer. Nick Xenophon expressed sadness but predicted this is not the end of Kakoschke-Moore's political career."
